<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="044" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>The Signal / Decision Record core pair is written whole, and only by the server and the ledger writers, on every path (owner 2026-11-04)</title>
    <phase>2 W2 Unified RecordCreationService (follow-up)</phase>
    <gate>042c merged to master; the dev import gated on the owner's go given in unified-access-control-r2's session</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Field security on four columns (solution XML), a change to CallerWriteAuthorization's field-security step (.cs, bff-api), a deploy and a live check (tags security, dataverse, deploy).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive column security across two owning projects (UAC-r2 owns profiles, ontology-r1 owns the tables and writers); must stay consistent with the owner's D-204 decision (the general create refuses these tables).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits CallerWriteAuthorization.cs, which 042c and 045 also touch; runs after 042c, before 045.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>042c</deps>
    <tags>dataverse, solution, fields, security, bff-api, deploy, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-10 hours (plus the review and gate wait)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make the core pair (sprk_corerecordtype, a lookup to sprk_recordtype_ref, plus sprk_corerecordid, a string) on sprk_signal and sprk_decisionrecord a server-written pair on every path: field-secure the four columns so that Create and Update are granted only to the BFF application identities, the ontology writer application identity and System Administrator, with Read unchanged for everyone; keep the service's own create of these rows working (042c's fill-or-clear, the caller's AppendTo on the core); and add the repair-pass backstop line to task 052. Design first, UAC-r2 reviews it, and the dev import waits for the owner's go in UAC-r2's session.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, Dataverse field-level security and the BFF write path. Security fails closed. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>On dev, the four columns are field-secured; the server create path and both ledger writers write the pair; every reader who reads the pair today still reads it; a guard keeps the solution XML, the profiles and the code in agreement.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>RE-SCOPED 2026-11-04 (owner decision, notes/decisions.md "created only by their writers", ontology D-204): the general create (RecordCreationService, chat create_record) refuses sprk_signal and sprk_decisionrecord as whole tables (042c fix round 4). So no service create of the core pair remains to keep working: the BFF-managed exemption in CallerWriteAuthorization step 3, AC4 and the fill-or-clear interplay are dropped; this task secures the columns for the writers' identities only. Re-confirm with UAC-r2 whether CallerWriteAuthorization needs any change at all. Original background: owner decision 3 of 2026-11-04 (notes/decisions.md): a half core pair must never be written on any path; the server fills the id from the derived root or clears the stray type with a warning (042c). This task covers the paths outside the server. UAC-r2 conditions of 2026-11-04 (coordinator relay): the profile design and a Grep proof go to UAC-r2 before any import; the dev apply needs the owner's go given in UAC-r2's session. Escalation owners: UAC-r2 owns roles and field security profiles; spaarke-ontology-platform-r1 owns both tables and their writers (decisions.md 2026-11-02, "Ontology-r1 research").</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/Entities/sprk_Signal/Entity.xml (sprk_CoreRecordId ~:491, sprk_CoreRecordType ~:531: IsSecured 0 to 1)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/Entities/sprk_DecisionRecord/Entity.xml (sprk_CoreRecordId ~:717, sprk_CoreRecordType ~:757)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/Other/FieldSecurityProfiles.xml (readers ~:3 "Spaarke BFF-Managed Field Readers": read 4; writers ~:471 "Spaarke BFF-Managed Field Writers" and ~:1163 "Spaarke Ontology Writer Field Writers": read/create/update 4)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CallerWriteAuthorization.cs (step 3, ~:92-113: the core pair of these two tables joins the BFF-managed exemption, the #1616 shape)</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/tasks/052-repair-pass-scheduled-job.poml (the 044(d) line, added at task-create 2026-11-04; confirm it still reads right after 042c)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/Signals/CorePairFieldSecurityAgreementTests.cs (solution XML, profiles and code agree)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">#1616 precedent: SecureRootInheritance.BffManagedPairTables (~:484), OwnedChildWrite.BffManagedPairColumnsOf (~:365), CallerWriteAuthorization step 3 (~:92-97), scripts/Set-RegardingPairFieldSecurity.ps1, tests/integration/data-mutation/ExternalAccess/RegardingPairFieldSecurityScriptAgreementTests.cs: copy the shape</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/CreatorPersonColumnSecuredGuardTests.cs and tests/integration/data-mutation/Signals/FirmReasonFieldSecurityAgreementTests.cs: secured-column agreement guards over the same solution files</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">Server writers of the pair (read only): Services/Signals/SignalWriter.cs, DecisionRecordWriter.cs, DecisionCommitService.cs, SignalSuppressionService.cs, Services/Ontology/OntologyAdminAuthoringService.cs; RecordCreationService (042c)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="042c" status="required">The general-create refusal of these tables (D-204) and the server-writer ArchTest (any server writer of the type also writes the id).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha 2026-10-20">Brief line 1: `git switch -c task/fm-044 &lt;tip of work/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1&gt;` (must contain 042c's merge), then confirm this POML exists on the branch.</constraint>
    <constraint source="UAC-r2 2026-11-04">Profile design (closed): Create and Update on the four columns for the BFF application identities and the ontology writer application identity (through the writer profiles above) and System Administrator; Read for everyone who reads today (the readers profile is associated with every business unit default team). No other principal gains or loses a column grant. The design and the Grep proof (AC2) go to UAC-r2 for review BEFORE any import.</constraint>
    <constraint source="UAC-r2 2026-11-04 (gate)">The dev import runs only after the owner's go, given in unified-access-control-r2's session, is recorded in the notes with its date. Without it the task stops at "ready to import". No other environment in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-11-04 / 042c (SUPERSEDED by D-204: the general create refuses these tables, so this exemption is not needed; kept for history)">A chat or route create of a Signal or Decision Record that sends a core pair keeps 042c's outcome after the columns are secured: step 3 treats the two core columns of these two tables as BFF-managed (the server asks the caller's AppendTo on the core before writing it), exactly as #1616 treats a project's pair. No refusal kind, code or word changes (NFR-07).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1">SignalWriter, DecisionRecordWriter and the other ontology writers are not changed. Adding the four columns to "Spaarke Ontology Writer Field Writers" needs ontology-r1's written agreement in the notes before the import.</constraint>
    <constraint source="confidentiality (repo is public)">Notes, PR text and commits state the goal positively ("the core pair is written only by the server"). If the Grep finds a client writer, report it to UAC-r2 in its session; do not describe it in the repo.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">No plugin, business rule or flow. Deploy via the dataverse-deploy skill only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">KEEP paths only (tests/integration/**, tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/**); no new file under tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/**.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Placement and publish delta: see notes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/decisions.md (2026-11-02 ontology research; 2026-11-04 sections)</file>
      <file>projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/task-042c-notes.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md (I-6, I-18)</file>
